  "summary": "17 published items, no preprints, code or industry records, rise ratio 2.86, zero 7-day star gain; work centres on tumor macrophage and T-cell immunity.",
  "synthesis": "The cluster consists of 17 published items with no preprint, code, or industry records. Content concentrates on tumor immune microenvironments: TREM2+ and TIMD4+ macrophages in intrahepatic cholangiocarcinoma, and TREM2+ macrophage-driven Treg recruitment via CCL5/CCL22 in lung adenocarcinoma; PLA1A-linked M2-like polarization in colorectal cancer; LAIR1 suppression of phagocytosis in glioma microglia/macrophages; and GULP1-driven anti-PD-1 resistance via CD36+ PD-L1+ TAMs in gastric cancer. T-cell-directed work includes histone lactylation expanding exhausted CD8+ T cells in glioblastoma, XIAP inhibition with a neoantigen vaccine in HCC, and IL-15 restoration of group 1 ILCs in brain metastasis. Several items are reviews or computational frameworks. The signal shows a 2.86 rise ratio with zero 7-day star gain; the items do not establish what drives this increase.",
